[38;5;252m[1m## Handling the allocator-dependent path[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;10mcompare_allocations[0m branches on the relative addresses of two independent [38;5;10mmalloc(4)[0m calls, and [38;5;10marity4[0m folds that into its return value. Its result is a deterministic function of process-wide heap state, not of the arguments — so calling C and Rust back-to-back in one process compares two different heap states and proves nothing. Instead each side runs in a freshly spawned child that [38;5;10mdlopen[0ms both libraries in the same order and invokes only one, then the parent compares the dumps byte-for-byte (after first asserting each side is reproducible across processes). The dump is 2883 lines and exercises all four [38;5;10mcompare_allocations[0m outcomes (1, 2, 11, 12) and 236 distinct [38;5;10marity4[0m results.[0m[0m
